123:     public static Color FromHsl(float hue, float saturation, float lightness);  // Requires color library
124:     public static Color FromHsluv(float hue, float saturation, float lightness); // Requires color library
125:     
126:     // Conversion operators
127:     public static implicit operator Color((byte r, byte g, byte b) rgb) => Rgb(rgb.r, rgb.g, rgb.b);
128:     public static implicit operator Color(byte[] rgb) => Rgb(rgb[0], rgb[1], rgb[2]); // Length 3 or 4
129: }
130: ```
131: 
132: #### Color String Parsing Requirements
133: 
134: The color parsing must support all formats used by Ratatui:
135: 
136: 1. **ANSI Color Names**: Case-insensitive, with comprehensive alias support
137:    - Standard: "red", "green", "blue", etc.
138:    - Bright variants: "lightred", "light red", "light-red", "light_red", "brightred", "bright red"
139:    - Aliases: "grey"/"gray", "silver" → Gray, "lightblack" → DarkGray, "lightwhite"/"lightgray" → White
140: 
141: 2. **Hex RGB Colors**: "#RRGGBB" format (case-insensitive)
142:    - Examples: "#FF0000", "#00ff00", "#0000FF"
143: 
144: 3. **Indexed Colors**: Numeric string "0" to "255"
145:    - Examples: "10", "42", "255"
146: 
147: 4. **Normalization Rules**:
148:    - Remove spaces, hyphens, underscores: "light-red" → "lightred"
149:    - Convert "bright" → "light": "brightred" → "lightred"
150:    - Handle spelling variants: "grey" → "gray"
151: 
152: #### Color Serialization Support (Optional Feature)
153: 
154: When JSON serialization is needed:
155: 
156: ```csharp
157: [JsonConverter(typeof(ColorJsonConverter))]
158: public readonly struct Color
159: {
160:     // Implementation...
161: }
162: 
163: public class ColorJsonConverter : JsonConverter<Color>
164: {
165:     public override Color Read(ref Utf8JsonReader reader, Type typeToConvert, JsonSerializerOptions options)
166:     {
167:         if (reader.TokenType == JsonTokenType.String)
168:         {
169:             return Color.Parse(reader.GetString()!);
170:         }
171:         
172:         // Support legacy format: {"Rgb": [255, 0, 0]} or {"Indexed": 10}
173:         // Implementation for backward compatibility...
174:     }
175:     
176:     public override void Write(Utf8JsonWriter writer, Color value, JsonSerializerOptions options)
177:     {
178:         writer.WriteStringValue(value.ToString());
179:     }
180: }
181: ```
